"The write model and read workloads are substantially different, and the read side can tolerate eventual consistency. I'll use CQRS."
Then explain:
Command side:
PostgreSQL + domain model

Synchronization:
Transactional Outbox + Kafka

Query side:
purpose-specific projections

Search:
OpenSearch

Dashboard:
analytical projection
That's much stronger than pattern-name dropping.
