41. What should you remember from Lesson 2?
I would want you to be able to explain these without memorizing definitions:
Event
Immutable business fact
Stream
Ordered event history for an aggregate
Stream version
Position of an event inside that aggregate's stream
Expected version
The version against which my business decision was made
Optimistic concurrency
Append only if the stream hasn't changed since I read it
Atomic append
The events produced by one aggregate decision are committed together
Global position
Position of an event across the broader event log/store
Event Store
Durable, ordered, append-oriented storage
with stream and concurrency semantics
