22. A robust payment flow
Let's design one.
Client generates:
OP-123
Request:
POST /payments
Idempotency-Key: OP-123
Payment service:
1. Validate request
2. Atomically claim OP-123
3. Create payment PAY-456
4. Call provider with provider key
5. Persist provider result
6. Mark OP-123 COMPLETED
7. Return result
Conceptually:
Client
  |
  | OP-123
  v
Payment Service
  |
  | claim
  v
DB
  |
  | PAY-456
  v
Provider
  |
  | provider-key = PAY-456
  v
Payment Network
Now retries can use:
OP-123
and provider retries can use:
PAY-456
These are different layers of identity.
