25. Why UNKNOWN deserves its own state
Consider:
SUCCESS
You know the operation happened.
FAILURE
You know it didn't happen.
But:
UNKNOWN
means:
We cannot currently prove either outcome.
That's a real business state.
This is a profound distributed-systems idea.
You don't always get:
true / false
Sometimes you get:
I don't know.
And a production system must know how to operate safely in that state.
